Device update omission and explicit null
========================================

PATCH device requests may omit name, is_active and is_managed to leave those
values unchanged. Explicit null is rejected with field validation status 422
before the update reaches PostgreSQL NOT NULL constraints. Previously those
inputs produced status 500. Invalid mixed requests do not partially change the
device. Empty PATCH requests keep existing behavior.

The request schema and generated frontend types show these fields as optional
but non-null. Name length limits remain 1..255. Existing boolean coercion is not
changed; false is a valid explicit update. Location, floor, room, notes and
credential_id remain nullable so callers can clear them. Organization, site,
permission and credential-reference checks remain in the endpoint.

Tests use real PostgreSQL rows and HTTP-ASGI plus a separate TCP HTTP probe.
They check explicit null, mixed requests, omission, false values, existing boolean
coercion, invalid lengths/values, missing credentials and clearing nullable data.
Stored state is checked after each response. OpenAPI checks preserve the name
limits and distinguish omitted fields from null. The authenticated principal is
synthetic; this is not real-login or concurrent-revocation qualification.

Only the DeviceUpdate schema, its generated frontend contract and associated
regression checks change. No migration, database data rewrite or hardware
operation occurs. Fresh frontend lint, tests and strict build are required for
the changed types; shipping/runtime qualification is separately recorded.

